{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DPoP"},{"type":"text","text":" header a caller presented, decide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether it proves possession for "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}]},{"type":"text","text":" request and "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" access token, and return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the key thumbprint that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)"},{"type":"text","text":" then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matches against the token’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.jkt"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","text":"Why this lives in the SDK","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success.”","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guarding an endpoint.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two most often missing: "},{"code":"typ","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — without pinning it to "},{"code":"dpop+jwt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", any "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"other","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" JWT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"ath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held by the same key."}]},{"anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg: none"},{"type":"text","text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token"}]},{"type":"text","text":". This enum dispatches on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"embedded key’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"crv"},{"type":"text","text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header says."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"